abstract: "A bounded Rust continuity experiment using the actual source-derived ESS-MAI PD engine and selected operational contracts with a new POC storage adapter. Local validation comprises 35 passing tests: 20 retained source unit tests and 15 integration tests. Five-turn and 65-turn experiments compare exact checkpoint bytes between uninterrupted execution and fresh-process continuation. Tests exercise retries, scoped head checks, corruption, incomplete tails and file ownership. The adapter is not the original KnowledgeVault or WAL-compatible with it. Valid rollback is accepted, finite bounds and source-version pinning remain explicit, and no science query or native knowledge verdict is produced. AI-assisted engineering and documentation are disclosed."
